## 4. Definitions

### 4.1 "LaLibertia"

"LaLibertia" means the parent brand under which the applicable work is produced, distributed, developed, or licensed.

### 4.2 "LaLibertiaDev"

"LaLibertiaDev" means the current owner/operator issuing this License on behalf of LaLibertia.

### 4.3 "Licensee"

"Licensee" means the person, company, organization, client, developer, or other recipient that legitimately obtains a Project or Material from LaLibertia / LaLibertiaDev or from a source authorized to distribute it.

The term "Licensee" includes a purchaser and, where applicable, an authorized recipient of a free Project. A person or entity that obtains a copy of a Project without such authorization (for example, through unauthorized copying, distribution, or access) is not a Licensee, does not receive any rights under this License, and remains subject to whatever legal remedies are available to LaLibertia / LaLibertiaDev and any affected third parties.

### 4.4 "Buyer"

"Buyer" means a Licensee that obtained the applicable Project through a commercial purchase or other paid transaction.

Where the context involves a free Project, "Licensee" or "Recipient" may be used instead.

### 4.5 "Project"

"Project" means the specific software, application, website, bot, tool, system, source code, design implementation, design file, UI/UX work, template, documentation, graphic, digital product, or other deliverable to which this License is expressly attached or designated.

### 4.6 "Material"

"Material" means any individual component, file, code, design, documentation, graphic, asset, or other work contained within or distributed with a Project.

### 4.7 "Source Code"

"Source Code" means editable source code delivered as part of the applicable Project, including frontend, backend, scripts, configuration, utilities, and other editable programming materials.

### 4.8 "Design Files"

"Design Files" means editable design materials, including Figma files and files created using other design platforms.

### 4.9 "Third-Party Material"

"Third-Party Material" means software, libraries, frameworks, fonts, icons, images, videos, plugins, APIs, services, models, tools, or other Materials not owned or controlled by LaLibertia / LaLibertiaDev.

### 4.10 "Purchase Agreement"

"Purchase Agreement" means an invoice, quotation, order, proposal, contract, marketplace transaction, written commercial agreement, or other documented arrangement governing a specific Project, if one exists. If no separate Purchase Agreement exists for a Project, this License governs that Project on its own, subject to applicable law.

### 4.11 "Project-Specific Agreement"

"Project-Specific Agreement" means a written agreement specifically identifying a Project and expressly modifying or supplementing this License.

