## 7. Prohibited Uses

Unless expressly authorized in writing by LaLibertia / LaLibertiaDev, the Licensee may not:

### 7.1 Resell Source Code

Sell, lease, sublicense, distribute, publish, or give away the Source Code as a standalone product.

### 7.2 Redistribute the Project

Distribute the Project or substantially similar Source Code or Design Files to unrelated third parties for the purpose of allowing those parties to obtain or reuse the underlying source.

### 7.3 Sell as a Template

Convert the Project into:

- a website template;
- software template;
- starter kit;
- boilerplate;
- UI kit;
- design kit;
- component library;
- Figma template;
- design asset;
- source-code package;
- marketplace product; or
- substantially similar reusable commercial product

for distribution to unrelated third parties.

### 7.4 Create a Competing Source Product

The Licensee may not take the Project or substantial portions of it and create a competing product whose primary value is providing substantially the same Source Code or Design Files to other customers.

### 7.5 Sublicense

The Licensee may not grant unrelated third parties a license that is broader than the Licensee's own rights.

### 7.6 Claim Ownership of Third-Party Material

The Licensee may not claim ownership of Third-Party Material merely because it is included in the Project.

### 7.7 Redistribute LaLibertia Internal Systems

The Licensee may not separately distribute LaLibertia's unrelated:

- internal libraries;
- internal tools;
- reusable systems;
- proprietary components;
- private templates;
- design systems;
- development frameworks; or
- internal documentation.

### 7.8 Misrepresent Creation

The Licensee may not knowingly and misleadingly claim that the Licensee independently created every part of the Project from scratch when that statement would be materially false.

The Licensee may, however, present the completed Project as its own deployed product, commissioned work, business system, or modified product where appropriate.

### 7.9 Grant Broader Rights

The Licensee may not grant another party rights exceeding the rights granted under this License.

