5. Keep a copy of the exact License version delivered with the Project.
6. Do not assume that payment automatically transfers copyright ownership.
7. Do not assume that public availability means open-source licensing.
8. Do not remove or alter third-party license notices where their licenses require them to remain.
9. Do not include private credentials, secrets, or confidential information in publicly distributed repositories.
10. Use the License version applicable to the Project rather than silently replacing the terms of an already-issued Project.

